README.md-9-cross-platform GPU terminal / agentic shell host. ScoreView renders MusicXML piano
README.md-10-scores with an embedded, pinned Verovio 6.2.1 engraving engine, drives them with a
README.md-11-transport clock, judges live playing from a MIDI keyboard, the microphone, or a dev
README.md-12-keyboard, and adapts the practice program to the player. The end goal, set out in
README.md-13-[plans/scoreview-manifesto.md](plans/scoreview-manifesto.md), is an adaptive
README.md:14:piano-learning experience — an "endless runner" practice stream that teaches the
README.md-15-piece you chose without ever feeling like practice.
README.md-16-
README.md-17-![Grieg's Waltz Op. 12, No. 2 rendered in ScoreView](screenshots/score.png)
README.md-18-
README.md:19:*ScoreView's reading view renders MusicXML as crisp, dynamically annotated notation.*
README.md-20-
README.md-21-![ScoreView adaptive player and learning inspector](screenshots/player.png)
README.md-22-
README.md-23-*The adaptive player combines a piano-roll guide with live performance analysis,
README.md-24-trouble spots, and the composer's evolving practice program.*
