README.md-36-
README.md:37:`source` accepts `.musicxml` or compressed `.mxl`; `mode` defaults to `paged`, with
README.md:38:`flow`, `flow-autoplay`, `roll`, and the runner tokens selecting conveyor/practice
README.md-39-behavior. Hidden panes pause the transport and release device leases by default;
README.md-40-`"background_playback": true` opts into hidden logic and audio (renders stay
README.md-41-suspended). The full product narrative lives in [docs/scoreview.md](docs/scoreview.md).
README.md-42-
README.md-43-## Facilities
--
README.md-45-- **Notation** — MusicXML/`.mxl` import through a semantic model with exact rational
README.md-46-  onsets and stable note ids (`product/draxul-notation`), engraved by a pinned
README.md-47-  Verovio 6.2.1. Verovio's SVG dialect is interpreted into a resolution-independent
README.md-48-  draw list (SMuFL glyph outlines, exact paths for staff lines/stems/beams/slurs,
README.md-49-  styled text runs) and replayed each frame — crisp at any DPI, clipped to its pane.
README.md:50:- **Viewing modes** — `paged` reading view with scrolling, zoom, and a status bar;
README.md-51-  `flow` conveyor mode that re-engraves the piece as one endless system under a
README.md:52:  settling playhead; `roll`, the runner: the transport never waits, each note judges
README.md-53-  in a timing window, and tempo eases up or down from demonstrated accuracy. A
README.md-54-  `gate` (wait) mode survives as a dev/verification instrument.
README.md-55-- **Playback and transport** — position-locked metronome with accented downbeats and
README.md-56-  eighth subdivisions, tempo control clamped to the piece's marking, and optional
README.md-57-  audition of the score through either a built-in synth or any `.sf2` soundfont
--
README.md-70-  chord drills, phrase-aware mastery gates, overnight re-tests), piece analysis
README.md-71-  (key estimation, chord inventory, motif mining, phrase/section structure) with an
README.md-72-  on-score overlay, spelling-based note coloring with a guidance keyboard and a
README.md-73-  piano-roll waterfall, and wrong-note marking on the sheet.
README.md-74-- **ImGui learning inspector** — a floating panel (self-hosted ImGui context) for
README.md:75:  transport, view toggles, audio, live performance stats, timing drift, the trouble
README.md-76-  tree, and the composer's upcoming program, drawn by the plugin's own
README.md-77-  Vulkan/Metal-backed renderer. Product preferences are pane-local.
README.md-78-- **Device discipline** — output, microphone, and named MIDI devices use
README.md-79-  process-local leases; passive panes never enumerate or open devices, and a lease
README.md-80-  conflict degrades to keyboard/visual operation with an actionable status.
--
