plans\scoreview-stream.md-10-notes succeeded, notes missed, chords in trouble, and — very important —
plans\scoreview-stream.md-11-timing tendencies (e.g. triplets consistently played slow must be
plans\scoreview-stream.md-12-detected, drilled, and fixed). The stream converges on the actual piece
plans\scoreview-stream.md-13-— beginning, middle, end, sliced and rearranged — **only as the player
plans\scoreview-stream.md-14-improves**: convergence is gated on demonstrated mastery, never on
plans\scoreview-stream.md:15:elapsed time. How long that takes varies per player and per piece; a
plans\scoreview-stream.md-16-session (or many) may never reach the full performance, and that's
plans\scoreview-stream.md-17-correct behavior — the problems get drilled until they're consistently
plans\scoreview-stream.md-18-right, and *getting* to the whole piece is the goal, not the schedule.
